 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? You' using a good webcam, so the basics are already covered. The main thing is to shoot with good lighting and a quiet room. Try sitting in front of a window so the light is coming from side and not directly in front of the camera. Also, close the curtains so the glare stops. Try to sit near a window so the sound carries well, but not so close that the cold air from the window makes the room cold. A small room with a window is often the winner. Shoot straight at the camera, so it looks like you' talking to someone face to face. Don't tilt it up or down.",
